der_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Erasca, Inc., a clinical-stage precision oncology company, focuses on discovering, developing, and commercializing therapies for patients with RAS/MAPK pathway-driven cancers. The company's product pipeline includes ERAS-0015, a pan-RAS molecular glue for the treatment of patients with RAS-mutated solid tumors; ERAS-4001, a pan-KRAS inhibitor for the treatment of patients with KRAS-mutated solid tumors; and ERAS-12, an investigational EGFR D2/D3 biparatopic antibody (bpAb) for the treatment of EGFR and RAS/MAPK solid tumors. It has license agreement with Guangzhou Joyo Pharmatech Co., Ltd to develop, manufacture, and commercialize certain pan-RAS inhibitors; Medshine Discovery Inc. to develop, manufacture, and commercialize certain pan-KRAS inhibitors; Novartis Pharma AG to develop, manufacture, use, and commercialize naporafenib; NiKang Therapeutics, Inc. to develop and commercialize ERAS-601 and certain other related compounds; and Asana BioSciences, LLC to develop and commercialize ERAS-007 and certain other related compounds. The company has a clinical trial collaboration and supply agreement with Tango Therapeutics, Inc. for the evaluation of ERAS-0015. Erasca, Inc. was incorporated in 2018 and is headquartered in San Diego, California.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Jonathan E. Lim M.D. | Co-Founder, Chairman & CEO | Age 53 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 103 people. Stock-based compensation of $242K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Erasca, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $5.0B market cap.","Returns on capital run at -235% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $96M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 6.0% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.7% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $2.3M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-2283572.0},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 292% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Erasca (ERAS) Could Be 45% Undervalued On New Cancer Trial